From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 07:59:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] audio: report the primary output's position from its device

The primary stream reports the frames its client has written as its
position, because its pipe did not carry every frame to the device.
The output now writes every frame to its ALSA stream, so report that
stream's presentation position, as StreamAlsa does: the frames written
less those still in the ALSA ring, at the time ALSA measured them.
While ALSA has no position, before the stream runs or after an
underrun, the reply carries an unknown position, as StreamAlsa's does.
In standby, and for the input, the client's count stays.
---
 audio/aidl/default/primary/StreamPrimary.cpp | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/audio/aidl/default/primary/StreamPrimary.cpp b/audio/aidl/default/primary/StreamPrimary.cpp
index 43a99a4b828344ed1c669c34045e4aa3ff285e79..6c74ae917387c8a0ea62a713de066747561e8e0c 100644
--- a/audio/aidl/default/primary/StreamPrimary.cpp
+++ b/audio/aidl/default/primary/StreamPrimary.cpp
@@ -151,7 +151,12 @@ StreamPrimary::StreamPrimary(StreamContext* context, const Metadata& metadata)
     return ::android::OK;
 }
 
-::android::status_t StreamPrimary::refinePosition(StreamDescriptor::Position*) {
+::android::status_t StreamPrimary::refinePosition(StreamDescriptor::Position* position) {
+    // Every output frame reaches the device (see 'transfer'), so the output reports the
+    // presentation position of its ALSA stream, which leaves out the frames still in the ring.
+    if (!mIsInput && !isStubStreamOnWorker() && !mAlsaDeviceProxies.empty()) {
+        return StreamAlsaMonoPipe::refinePosition(position);
+    }
     // Since not all data is actually sent to the HAL, use the position maintained by Stream class
     // which accounts for all frames passed from / to the client.
     return ::android::OK;
